holds. We also denote D by (Zn2 kZn2 ) × Z2 since the two factors are diagonal.
    Figure 1 shows the situation involving Wn , N and D. Interestingly, the in-
tersection of N and D is the center ζ(Wn ) of Wn which coincides with the com-
