    Since D is abelian we can solve the hidden subgroup problem for D by the
usual abelian hidden subgroup algorithm. We do this by performing Hadamard
transforms on the qubits representing y and a followed by controlled NOTs be-
tween qubits xi and yi for i = 1, . . . , n (see figure (2)). This is followed by the
hidden subgroup algorithm for Zn+1
