                              DFTG∗ ·     Φ(t) · DFTZ2
                                        t∈T

provides a Fourier transform for G. Here Φ(t) denotes the extension (as a whole)
of the regular representation of G∗ to a representation of G (see [11], [2], [12]). In
case of Wn the transform DFTG∗ is the Fourier transform for Z2n    2 and therefore
a tensor product of 2n Hadamard matrices.
    The circuits for the case of Wn are shown in figure 3. Quantum circuits
